      "answer": "The regular **assessment period (*Festsetzungsfrist*) for income tax is four years** [4]. \n\n* **Statutory rule:** The period generally begins at the end of the calendar year in which the tax arose [2]. However, if a tax return (*Steuererklärung*) must be submitted, the period begins at the end of the calendar year in which the tax return is submitted, but **at the latest at the end of the third calendar year** following the year the tax arose (unless it begins later) [2]. \n* **Longer periods:** In cases of tax evasion (*Steuerhinterziehung*), the period is ten years, and for reckless tax shortening (*leichtfertige Steuerverkürzung*), it is five years [4]."
